        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The numbered ring is a torque limiter, the 1 and 2 are gears, the drill icon turns the clutch off and the hammer icon pounds masonry. Use a numbered clutch setting in gear 1 to drive screws, the drill icon to bore holes, and a quick test screw to find the right number for each new job. The battery numbers only tell you how long the session will last.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If your current drill makes the clutch hard to read, slips unpredictably or lacks a second gear, it may be time for an upgrade. Our cordless drill rankings call out which models have a clutch with fine, consistent steps, which is the feature that makes every number on this list easier to use.
          </p>
